---
// Agency partnership page (local-SEO brand profile + Minnesota Marketing / Dirtwork
// Digital aside). Built 2026-09-04 per Clients/Agency Page Standard & Ledger.md,
// "Division clients: the dual-link pattern". Not in the primary nav; reached from the
// footer credit on every page and from the sitemap.
//
// Link assignment (ledger row 7, do not change without updating the ledger):
//   Footer credit: "Site by Minnesota Marketing" -> this page (internal)
//   Link 1: "Dirtwork Digital, a Minnesota Marketing division" -> https://minnesotamarketing.com/dirtwork-digital
//   Link 2: "dirtworkdigital.com" -> https://www.dirtworkdigital.com/
//   Eyebrow: A MINNESOTA MARKETING PARTNERSHIP
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { img } from '../lib/images';
import { business, towns, counties } from '../data/site';

const heroImg = img('hero-fleet.jpg');
const aerialImg = img('aerial-yard-laporte.jpg');
const crewImg = img('crew.jpg');

const slug = 'excavation-and-septic-contractor-laporte-minnesota';
const canonical = `${business.domain}/${slug}`;
const title = 'Excavation & Septic Contractor in Laporte, MN | Shepard';
const description =
  'Shepard Excavating and Septic Service is a family-owned septic, excavating, gravel, and snow removal contractor in Laporte, MN, serving the northern lakes since 1997.';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${business.domain}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Septic and Excavation Contractor in Laporte, MN', item: canonical },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} ogImage="/og/laporte-mn.jpg" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="agency">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="ag-hero" aria-label="Shepard Excavating in Laporte, Minnesota">
      <Image src={heroImg} alt="Shepard Excavating truck fleet at the shop in Laporte, MN" class="ag-hero-bg" widths={[768, 1280, 1920]} sizes="100vw" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" quality={76} />
      <div class="ag-hero-overlay"></div>
      <div class="container ag-hero-inner">
        <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Laporte, MN</span></nav>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Shepard Excavating &middot; Laporte, MN</p>
        <h1>Septic and excavation contractor serving Laporte, Minnesota and the northern lakes</h1>
        <p class="ag-lead">A family-run outfit on County 45 in Laporte that has been pumping, digging, hauling, and plowing across Beltrami, Hubbard, and Cass counties since {business.founded}.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Body -->
    <div class="section ag-body">
      <div class="container ag-prose">

        <section class="ag-section">
          <p class="eyebrow">Who we are</p>
          <h2>A family-owned septic and dirt-work company in Laporte</h2>
          <p>Shepard Excavating and Septic Service, LLC is a family-owned contractor based in Laporte, Minnesota. Brian Shepard has run the company since {business.founded}, and when you call, you reach the people whose name is on the truck. The business does two things most contractors split between separate companies: septic work and dirt work.</p>
          <p>On the septic side that means routine pumping, inspections, line cleaning, and new mound or conventional systems designed and installed to code. On the dirt side it means basements, foundations, driveways, site prep, land clearing, demolition, and sand and gravel picked up at the pit or delivered to the job. Add snow removal and a Fisher snowplow dealership, and Shepard is the one call that covers a lake property from the first shovel to the last snowfall.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="ag-section">
          <p class="eyebrow">Community roots</p>
          <h2>Three decades of work in Northern Minnesota lake country</h2>
          <p>Laporte sits between Bemidji and Walker on the edge of the Chippewa National Forest, in the middle of the lake country Shepard has worked for nearly thirty years. The crew knows what a tight cabin lot on Garfield Lake needs, how a rural driveway holds up through a Northern Minnesota freeze, and which county office handles a new septic permit in Hubbard versus Beltrami County. That local knowledge shows up in the details: a septic design that fits the soil on a lake lot, a driveway that drains, a demolition that is hauled away clean.</p>
          <p>The company is licensed to install and maintain septic systems in Hubbard and Beltrami counties and holds MPCA certification as a subsurface sewage treatment system installer. Customers around Laporte, Bemidji, Park Rapids, Walker, Cass Lake, Hackensack, and Longville have relied on that combination of licensing and local experience since {business.founded}, and many of the reviews on this site come from repeat customers who call the same crew year after year.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="ag-section">
          <p class="eyebrow">What we do</p>
          <h2>Septic, excavating, materials, and winter work under one roof</h2>
          <p>Because septic, excavating, materials, and winter work all live under one roof in Laporte, property owners skip juggling four contractors for one job. Shepard's services include:</p>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><a href="/septic-pumping">Septic pumping</a>, inspections, and maintenance, including frozen line steaming and rooter service</li>
            <li><a href="/septic-system">Septic system design and installation</a> (mound and conventional), county permitting, and final inspection</li>
            <li><a href="/excavating">Excavating</a> for basements, foundations, site prep, grading, and road building</li>
            <li><a href="/land-clearing">Land clearing</a>, tree and stump removal for new builds and lake lots</li>
            <li><a href="/demolition">Demolition</a> of cabins, garages, and small commercial structures, hauled away clean</li>
            <li><a href="/aggregate">Sand, gravel, and aggregate</a>: fill sand, screened topsoil, Class 5, crushed concrete, washed rock, and boulders, picked up at the pit or delivered and spread</li>
            <li><a href="/snow-removal">Snow removal</a> for driveways and commercial lots</li>
            <li><a href="/fisher-snowplows">Fisher snowplow</a> and salter sales, parts, and service, ordered year-round</li>
          </ul>
          <figure class="ag-figure">
            <Image src={aerialImg} alt="Aerial view of the Shepard Excavating yard and aggregate piles in Laporte, MN" widths={[700, 1200, 1600]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 820px" quality={76} loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>The Shepard yard on County 45 in Laporte, with sand, gravel, and crushed material ready for pickup or delivery.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </section>

        <section class="ag-section">
          <p class="eyebrow">Good questions</p>
          <h2>What Laporte-area customers ask before they call</h2>
          <p>Most calls to the Laporte shop start with the same handful of questions:</p>
          <ul class="ag-qa">
            <li><strong>Is it Shepard or Shepherd Excavating?</strong> The family name is Shepard, but plenty of people write Shepherd. Both point to the same business in Laporte, MN.</li>
            <li><strong>How often should a septic tank be pumped?</strong> Every two to three years for most Northern Minnesota households. Shepard can put you on a maintenance schedule so you do not have to keep track.</li>
            <li><strong>Are you a licensed septic installer?</strong> Yes. MPCA-certified, with more than 20 years installing systems, handling the design, county permits, installation, and final inspection.</li>
            <li><strong>Can you thaw a frozen septic or water line?</strong> Yes. The crew steams frozen lines and clears sewer backups with rooter and line-cleaning equipment during business hours.</li>
            <li><strong>How much gravel or fill do I need?</strong> Use the free <a href="/material-calculator">Material Calculator</a> for a cubic-yard estimate before you order, then call for delivery.</li>
            <li><strong>What areas do you serve?</strong> Beltrami, Hubbard, and Cass counties, including Bemidji, Laporte, Park Rapids, Walker, Cass Lake, Hackensack, and Longville.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="ag-section">
          <p class="eyebrow">What sets Shepard apart</p>
          <h2>Licensed septic installation and a Fisher snowplow dealership</h2>
          <p>Two things set Shepard apart in the Laporte and Bemidji market. The first is the septic license itself. Shepard is an MPCA-certified installer and a licensed installer and maintainer in both Hubbard and Beltrami counties, so a new mound system on a lake lot is designed, permitted, installed, and inspected by one company. The tagline "We're #1 in the #2 business" gets a laugh, but it reflects real specialization, and because the same crew pumps and maintains systems, they see what fails and why before they build yours.</p>
          <p>The second is the Fisher snowplow dealership. Shepard stocks v-plows and straight blades sized for half-ton pickups and ATVs, plus salters, and can order plows year-round so customers are ready before the first storm hits Northern Minnesota. Between those two lines, the free online Material Calculator, and a yard full of sand and gravel on County 45, the company offers things a general excavator in the region usually cannot.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="ag-section">
          <p class="eyebrow">How to get started</p>
          <h2>Working with Shepard: a phone call or a short form</h2>
          <p>Getting started is a phone call or a short form. Customers in the Laporte area call <a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phone}</a> during business hours, Monday through Friday, 7:00am to 5:00pm, or submit the estimate request form on the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> with their name, phone, service address, and the service they need. The request lands directly with the office, and the follow-up is a clear estimate and an honest timeline.</p>
          <p>Septic pumping and line service are scheduled quickly, often for the next business day. Larger excavation, septic installation, and demolition projects start with a site visit so the crew can look at access, soil, and permit requirements before quoting. Aggregate can be picked up at the yard near Laporte or delivered and spread on site.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="ag-section">
          <p class="eyebrow">Why it matters</p>
          <h2>Why a licensed local contractor matters on a Northern Minnesota lake lot</h2>
          <p>Septic and excavation work in Northern Minnesota is not a job for whoever owns a backhoe. Lake lots around Laporte, Walker, and Bemidji sit on mixed soils with high water tables, county setback rules, and a freeze that reaches deep into the ground every winter. A septic system that is undersized or badly sited fails early and can put a lake at risk. A driveway or building pad that is not graded for drainage heaves and washes out. A demolition that leaves debris behind becomes someone else's problem.</p>
          <p>Hiring a licensed, insured, local contractor protects the property owner on all of those fronts. For Laporte-area homeowners and cabin owners, that is the difference between a system and a site that last for decades and one that has to be redone.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Mid-page CTA card -->
    <section class="midcta" aria-label="Get a free estimate">
      <div class="container midcta-inner">
        <div class="midcta-copy">
          <h2>Got a project around Laporte? Let's talk.</h2>
          <p>Tell us what you are planning and we will get you a clear estimate and an honest timeline. No pressure, no runaround.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="midcta-actions">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Get a Free Estimate</a>
          <a href={business.phoneHref} class="btn btn-outline btn-lg">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6.6 10.8a15.5 15.5 0 0 0 6.6 6.6l2.2-2.2a1 1 0 0 1 1-.24 11.4 11.4 0 0 0 3.6.58 1 1 0 0 1 1 1V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1A17 17 0 0 1 3 4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h3.5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1c0 1.25.2 2.46.58 3.6a1 1 0 0 1-.25 1l-2.2 2.2Z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
            Call {business.phone}
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Visit / closing -->
    <section class="section section--stone">
      <div class="container ag-visit">
        <div class="ag-visit-text">
          <p class="eyebrow">Visit or call</p>
          <h2>Find Shepard Excavating in Laporte, Minnesota</h2>
          <p>Shepard Excavating and Septic Service is located at {business.address.street}, {business.address.city}, {business.address.region} {business.address.zip}, and serves {counties.slice(0, -1).join(', ')}, and {counties[counties.length - 1]} counties, including {towns.slice(0, -1).join(', ')}, and {towns[towns.length - 1]}. Office hours are Monday through Friday, 7:00am to 5:00pm; closed Saturday and Sunday.</p>
          <p>Call <a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phone}</a>, email <a href={business.emailHref}>{business.email}</a>, or visit the <a href="/laporte-mn">Laporte service page</a> and the <a href="/about">about page</a> to learn more about the crew.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="ag-visit-photo">
          <Image src={crewImg} alt="The Shepard Excavating and Septic Service team in front of a company truck" widths={[600, 1000]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 440px" quality={78} loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Agency aside -->
    <aside class="ag-partner" aria-label="Website and marketing partner">
      <div class="container ag-partner-inner">
        <p class="eyebrow ag-partner-eyebrow">A Minnesota Marketing Partnership</p>
        <h2>How Shepard Excavating supports its online presence</h2>
        <p>Shepard Excavating and Septic Service works with <a href="https://minnesotamarketing.com/dirtwork-digital" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dirtwork Digital, a Minnesota Marketing division</a> that builds websites only for excavation, septic, and sitework companies. The agency handled the website design and strategy behind shepardexcavating.com, rebuilding it in August 2026 as a fast site with a page for every service and town Shepard serves, plus the free Material Calculator. It manages the ongoing search engine optimization that helps Laporte-area customers find the company by need and not just by name, manages the Shepard Google Business Profile, and produces the drone videography and photography of the yard, the fleet, and septic jobs across the northern lakes. Ongoing hosting and care are handled by the same team at <a href="https://www.dirtworkdigital.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dirtworkdigital.com</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Hero (mirrors the about page hero) */
  .ag-hero { position: relative; isolation: isolate; display: flex; align-items: center; min-height: clamp(360px, 52vh, 520px); }
  .ag-hero :global(.ag-hero-bg) { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; z-index: -2; }
  .ag-hero-overlay { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: -1; background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(20,18,16,0.86) 0%, rgba(20,18,16,0.5) 60%, rgba(20,18,16,0.25) 100%), linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(20,18,16,0.7), rgba(20,18,16,0.2)); }
  .ag-hero-inner { color: #fff; padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); }
  .crumbs { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; font-family: var(--font-head); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.82rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #cfccc2; margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
  .crumbs a { color: var(--yellow); }
  .eyebrow--light { color: var(--yellow); }
  .eyebrow--light::before { background: var(--yellow); }
  .ag-hero h1 { color: #fff; margin-top: 0.5rem; max-width: 24ch; text-shadow: 0 2px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); }
  .ag-lead { max-width: 54ch; margin-top: 1rem; font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem); color: #ece9e2; }

  /* Long-form body */
  .ag-prose { max-width: 860px; }
  .ag-section + .ag-section { margin-top: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.4rem); }
  .ag-section h2 { margin-top: 0.6rem; font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem); }
  .ag-section p { color: var(--slate); margin-top: 0.9rem; max-width: 68ch; }
  .ag-section p a, .ag-visit-text p a, .ticks a { color: var(--red); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; font-weight: 700; }
  .ag-section p a:hover, .ag-visit-text p a:hover, .ticks a:hover { color: var(--red-deep); }

  .ticks { display: grid; gap: 0.6rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .ticks li { position: relative; padding-left: 1.6rem; color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.45; }
  .ticks li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.45em; width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--yellow); }

  .ag-qa { display: grid; gap: 0.9rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .ag-qa li { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-lg); padding: 1rem 1.2rem; color: var(--slate); line-height: 1.55; }
  .ag-qa li strong { display: block; font-family: var(--font-head); font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  .ag-qa a { color: var(--red); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; font-weight: 700; }

  .ag-figure { margin-top: 1.8rem; border-radius: var(--r-lg); overflow: hidden; box-shadow: var(--shadow); background: #fff; }
  .ag-figure :global(img) { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  .ag-figure figcaption { padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-family: var(--font-head); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--slate); }

  /* Mid CTA (same look as MidCTA.astro) */
  .midcta { background: var(--ink); color: #fff; border-top: 3px solid var(--yellow); }
  .midcta-inner { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1.8rem; flex-wrap: wrap; padding-block: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .midcta-copy { flex: 1 1 320px; }
  .midcta h2 { color: #fff; font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.2vw, 2.2rem); }
  .midcta p { color: #cfccc2; margin-top: 0.5rem; max-width: 52ch; }
  .midcta-actions { display: flex; gap: 0.8rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }

  /* Visit */
  .ag-visit { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr; gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); align-items: center; }
  .ag-visit-text h2 { margin-top: 0.6rem; font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem); }
  .ag-visit-text p { color: var(--slate); margin-top: 0.9rem; max-width: 60ch; }
  .ag-visit-photo { border-radius: var(--r-lg); overflow: hidden; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .ag-visit-photo :global(img) { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }

  /* Agency aside */
  .ag-partner { background: var(--charcoal); color: #f2f2f2; border-top: 4px solid var(--yellow); }
  .ag-partner-inner { max-width: 860px; padding-block: clamp(2.6rem, 5vw, 3.6rem); }
  .ag-partner-eyebrow { color: var(--yellow); }
  .ag-partner-eyebrow::before { background: var(--yellow); }
  .ag-partner h2 { color: #fff; margin-top: 0.6rem; font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6vw, 1.8rem); }
  .ag-partner p { color: #cfcfcf; margin-top: 0.9rem; max-width: 72ch; }
  .ag-partner a { color: #fff; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--yellow); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .ag-partner a:hover { color: var(--yellow); }

  @media (max-width: 900px) { .ag-visit { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .midcta-actions { width: 100%; }
    .midcta-actions .btn { flex: 1 1 100%; justify-content: center; }
  }
</style>
